# AWS lab credentials — copy to aws.env, paste your values, save. aws.env is git-ignored.
#
# This is the file the Week 15 technical demo uses on camera.
#
# Where the values come from: your AWS Lab Control Panel → Access Details
#   accessId   → AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
#   accessKey  → AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
# (Using your own AWS account instead? Same two values from your IAM user.)
#
# Load into the current shell:   set -a; source aws.env; set +a
# Verify:                        aws sts get-caller-identity     (prints your ARN)
#
# Two distinct failure signatures — believe the output over any assumption:
#   * "explicit deny" on bedrock:*        → the lab account's Start/Stop switch is off.
#   * "AccessDenied … because no identity-based policy allows" → that login has NO
#     Bedrock grants at all, and starting the lab does not change it. Use your own
#     AWS account for live Bedrock/AgentCore beats, or teach them with --mock.
#
# Prefer not to keep keys in a file? Leave this unused and configure `aws configure`
# (~/.aws) instead — every lab reads standard AWS credentials from the environment.
# The non-AWS knobs (portal URL, analyst API keys, Slack) live in .env.example.

AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=paste_accessId_here
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=paste_accessKey_here
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
